{"id":"mahabharata-3-245","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":245,"title":"पञ्चचत्वारिंशदधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 245 · Vyasa's visit: austerity and giving","summary":{"en":"In the eleventh year of exile Vyasa visits the Pandavas and consoles Yudhishthira, teaching that austerity and giving are the highest means and that what is given rightly bears fruit for ever. He begins the ancient tale of the sage Mudgala and the measure of rice.","kn":"ವನವಾಸದ ಹನ್ನೊಂದನೆಯ ವರ್ಷದಲ್ಲಿ ವ್ಯಾಸರು ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ಭೇಟಿಯಾಗಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನನ್ನು ಸಂತೈಸಿ, ತಪಸ್ಸು ದಾನಗಳೇ ಶ್ರೇಷ್ಠ ಸಾಧನಗಳು, ನ್ಯಾಯವಾಗಿ ಕೊಟ್ಟದ್ದು ಶಾಶ್ವತ ಫಲ ಕೊಡುತ್ತದೆ ಎಂದು ಉಪದೇಶಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಮುದ್ಗಲ ಋಷಿ ಮತ್ತು ದ್ರೋಣಮಾತ್ರ ಧಾನ್ಯದ ಪ್ರಾಚೀನ ಕಥೆಯನ್ನು ಆರಂಭಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"वनवास के ग्यारहवें वर्ष में व्यास पाण्डवों से मिलकर युधिष्ठिर को सान्त्वना देते हैं और सिखाते हैं कि तप और दान सर्वोत्तम साधन हैं और उचित रीति से दिया गया दान सदा फल देता है। वे ऋषि मुद्गल और द्रोण भर धान की प्राचीन कथा आरम्भ करते हैं।","te":"వనవాసపు పదకొండవ సంవత్సరంలో వ్యాసుడు పాండవులను సందర్శించి యుధిష్ఠిరుని ఓదార్చి, తపస్సు, దానమే శ్రేష్ఠ సాధనాలని, న్యాయంగా ఇచ్చినది శాశ్వత ఫలం ఇస్తుందని ఉపదేశిస్తాడు. ముద్గల మహర్షి, ద్రోణమాత్రం ధాన్యపు ప్రాచీన కథను ప్రారంభిస్తాడు.","ta":"வனவாசத்தின் பதினோராம் ஆண்டில் வியாசர் பாண்டவர்களைச் சந்தித்து யுதிஷ்டிரருக்கு ஆறுதல் சொல்லி, தவமும் கொடையுமே உயர்ந்த வழிகள், முறையாக அளித்தது என்றும் பலன் தரும் என்று உபதேசிக்கிறார். முத்கல முனிவரும் ஒரு த்ரோண அளவு நெல்லும் பற்றிய பழங்கதையைத் தொடங்குகிறார்.","ml":"പ്രവാസത്തിന്റെ പതിനൊന്നാം വർഷത്തിൽ വ്യാസൻ പാണ്ഡവരെ സന്ദർശിച്ച് യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ ആശ്വസിപ്പിക്കുന്നു; തപസ്സും ദാനവുമാണ് ഉന്നതമായ മാർഗ്ഗങ്ങളെന്നും, ശരിയായി നൽകുന്നത് എന്നേക്കും ഫലം നൽകുമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പഠിപ്പിക്കുന്നു. മുദ്ഗലമുനിയുടെയും ഒരു അളവ് അരിയുടെയും പുരാതന കഥ അദ്ദേഹം തുടങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.245; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"व्रीहिद्रौणिकपर्व","titleEn":"Vrihidraunika Parva (A measure of rice)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"वने निवसतां तेषां पाण्डवानां महात्मनाम् ।\nवर्षाण्येकादशातीयुः कृच्छ्रेण भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the great-souled Pandavas lived in the forest, eleven years passed with hardship, O bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":2,"text":"फलमूलाशनास्ते हि सुखार्हा दुःखमुत्तमम् ।\nप्राप्तकालमनुध्यान्तः सेहुरुत्तमपूरुषाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eating fruit and roots, those best of men, who deserved comfort, endured great suffering, watching for the time to come."}},{"n":3,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्तु राजर्षिरात्मकर्मापराधजम् ।\nचिन्तयन्स महाबाहुर्भ्रातॄणां दुःखमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The royal sage Yudhishthira, the mighty-armed one, brooded on the great grief of his brothers, caused by his own deeds."}},{"n":4,"text":"न सुष्वाप सुखं राजा हृदि शल्यैरिवार्पितैः ।\nदौरात्म्यमनुपश्यंस्तत्काले द्यूतोद्भवस्य हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king could not sleep in comfort, as if arrows were lodged in his heart, as he recalled the wickedness that arose from the dice game."}},{"n":5,"text":"संस्मरन्परुषा वाचः सूतपुत्रस्य पाण्डवः ।\nनिःश्वासपरमो दीनो बिभ्रत्कोपविषं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava remembered the harsh words of the charioteer's son, sighing heavily and wretched, holding in a great poison of anger."}},{"n":6,"text":"अर्जुनो यमजौ चोभौ द्रौपदी च यशस्विनी ।\nस च भीमो महातेजाः सर्वेषामुत्तमो बली ।\nयुधिष्ठिरमुदीक्षन्तः सेहुर्दुःखमनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, the twins, the famous Draupadi and mighty Bhima, strongest of all, looking to Yudhishthira, bore this supreme sorrow."}},{"n":7,"text":"अवशिष्टमल्पकालं मन्वानाः पुरुषर्षभाः ।\nवपुरन्यदिवाकार्षुरुत्साहामर्षचेष्टितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking that little time remained, those bulls among men seemed to take on a new form in their zeal and anger."}},{"n":8,"text":"कस्यचित्त्वथ कालस्य व्यासः सत्यवतीसुतः ।\nआजगाम महायोगी पाण्डवानवलोककः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After some time Vyasa, son of Satyavati, the great yogi, came to see the Pandavas."}},{"n":9,"text":"तमागतमभिप्रेक्ष्य कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nप्रत्युद्गम्य महात्मानं प्रत्यगृह्णाद्यथाविधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him arrive, Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, went out to meet the great one and received him with due ceremony."}},{"n":10,"text":"तमासीनमुपासीनः शुश्रूषुर्नियतेन्द्रियः ।\nतोषयन्प्रणिपातेन व्यासं पाण्डवनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The delight of the Pandavas, with controlled senses, sat near him as he sat and served him, pleasing Vyasa with a bow."}},{"n":11,"text":"तानवेक्ष्य कृशान्पौत्रान्वने वन्येन जीवतः ।\nमहर्षिरनुकम्पार्थमब्रवीद्बाष्पगद्गदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his grandsons lean, living on forest food in the forest, the great sage said, with a voice choked with tears, out of compassion:"}},{"n":12,"text":"युधिष्ठिर महाबाहो शृणु धर्मभृतां वर ।\nनातप्ततपसः पुत्र प्राप्नुवन्ति महत्सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Yudhishthira, mighty-armed, best of those who uphold dharma, listen. My son, those who have not practiced austerity do not gain great happiness."}},{"n":13,"text":"सुखदुःखे हि पुरुषः पर्यायेणोपसेवते ।\nनात्यन्तमसुखं कश्चित्प्राप्नोति पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man experiences happiness and sorrow in turn. No one, bull among men, gets unbroken misery."}},{"n":14,"text":"प्रज्ञावांस्त्वेव पुरुषः संयुक्तः परया धिया ।\nउदयास्तमयज्ञो हि न शोचति न हृष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"A wise man, with a superior mind, who knows rising and setting, neither grieves nor rejoices."}},{"n":15,"text":"सुखमापतितं सेवेद्दुःखमापतितं सहेत् ।\nकालप्राप्तमुपासीत सस्यानामिव कर्षकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should enjoy happiness when it comes and bear sorrow when it comes, and wait for the right time like a farmer for his crops."}},{"n":16,"text":"तपसो हि परं नास्ति तपसा विन्दते महत् ।\nनासाध्यं तपसः किंचिदिति बुध्यस्व भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is nothing higher than austerity; by austerity one gains greatness. Know, Bharata, that nothing is unattainable by austerity."}},{"n":17,"text":"सत्यमार्जवमक्रोधः संविभागो दमः शमः ।\nअनसूयाविहिंसा च शौचमिन्द्रियसंयमः ।\nसाधनानि महाराज नराणां पुण्यकर्मणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Truth, honesty, freedom from anger, sharing, self-control, peace, absence of envy, nonviolence, purity and restraint of the senses are, great king, the means of those who do good deeds."}},{"n":18,"text":"अधर्मरुचयो मूढास्तिर्यग्गतिपरायणाः ।\nकृच्छ्रां योनिमनुप्राप्य न सुखं विन्दते जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deluded people who like adharma and head for animal births get a hard birth and find no happiness."}},{"n":19,"text":"इह यत्क्रियते कर्म तत्परत्रोपभुज्यते ।\nतस्माच्छरीरं युञ्जीत तपसा नियमेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The deed done here is enjoyed in the next world; so one should discipline the body with austerity and restraint."}},{"n":20,"text":"यथाशक्ति प्रयच्छेच्च संपूज्याभिप्रणम्य च ।\nकाले पात्रे च हृष्टात्मा राजन्विगतमत्सरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should give as one can, with respect and a bow, at the right time and to the right person, with a glad heart, free from envy, O king."}},{"n":21,"text":"सत्यवादी लभेतायुरनायासमथार्जवी ।\nअक्रोधनोऽनसूयश्च निर्वृतिं लभते पराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who speaks truth gains long life; one who is honest, ease; one who is free of anger and envy gains great contentment."}},{"n":22,"text":"दान्तः शमपरः शश्वत्परिक्लेशं न विन्दति ।\nन च तप्यति दान्तात्मा दृष्ट्वा परगतां श्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A self-controlled man devoted to peace never suffers distress, and one with a controlled mind does not burn on seeing another's prosperity."}},{"n":23,"text":"संविभक्ता च दाता च भोगवान्सुखवान्नरः ।\nभवत्यहिंसकश्चैव परमारोग्यमश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who shares and gives becomes rich in enjoyment and happy, harmless, and gains perfect health."}},{"n":24,"text":"मान्यान्मानयिता जन्म कुले महति विन्दति ।\nव्यसनैर्न तु संयोगं प्राप्नोति विजितेन्द्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who honors those worthy of honor is born in a great family, and one who has conquered his senses does not meet with calamities."}},{"n":25,"text":"शुभानुशयबुद्धिर्हि संयुक्तः कालधर्मणा ।\nप्रादुर्भवति तद्योगात्कल्याणमतिरेव सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One with a mind set on good consequences, joined to the law of time, shows up with a mind set on welfare.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"भगवन्दानधर्माणां तपसो वा महामुने ।\nकिं स्विद्बहुगुणं प्रेत्य किं वा दुष्करमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Revered great sage, of the duties of giving and of austerity, which has more merit hereafter, and which is said to be harder?"}},{"text":"व्यास उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vyasa said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"दानान्न दुष्करतरं पृथिव्यामस्ति किंचन ।\nअर्थे हि महती तृष्णा स च दुःखेन लभ्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nothing on earth is harder than giving. Craving for wealth is great and it is gained with pain."}},{"n":28,"text":"परित्यज्य प्रियान्प्राणान्धनार्थं हि महाहवम् ।\nप्रविशन्ति नरा वीराः समुद्रमटवीं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men give up their dear lives for wealth, heroes enter great battles and the sea and the wilderness."}},{"n":29,"text":"कृषिगोरक्ष्यमित्येके प्रतिपद्यन्ति मानवाः ।\nपुरुषाः प्रेष्यतामेके निर्गच्छन्ति धनार्थिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some take up farming and cattle-keeping; others go out as servants, seeking wealth."}},{"n":30,"text":"तस्य दुःखार्जितस्यैवं परित्यागः सुदुष्करः ।\nन दुष्करतरं दानात्तस्माद्दानं मतं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving up what was won with such pain is very hard. Nothing is harder than giving, so I hold giving to be the highest."}},{"n":31,"text":"विशेषस्त्वत्र विज्ञेयो न्यायेनोपार्जितं धनम् ।\nपात्रे देशे च काले च साधुभ्यः प्रतिपादयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One thing must be understood here: wealth earned by just means should be given to good people at the right place, time and to a worthy recipient."}},{"n":32,"text":"अन्यायसमुपात्तेन दानधर्मो धनेन यः ।\nक्रियते न स कर्तारं त्रायते महतो भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The duty of giving done with wealth unjustly gained does not save the doer from great fear."}},{"n":33,"text":"पात्रे दानं स्वल्पमपि काले दत्तं युधिष्ठिर ।\nमनसा सुविशुद्धेन प्रेत्यानन्तफलं स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A gift to a worthy person, even a small one, given at the right time with a pure mind, Yudhishthira, is said to bear endless fruit hereafter."}},{"n":34,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nव्रीहिद्रोणपरित्यागाद्यत्फलं प्राप मुद्गलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this they tell an ancient tale, of the fruit that Mudgala obtained by giving up a drona of rice."}}]}]}